.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-invoices-void - Void an invoice


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago invoices void  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint is used for voiding an invoice.
• When no body parameters are provided, the invoice can be voided only if it is in a \fBfinalized\fR status and its payment status is NOT \fBsucceeded\fR\&.
• When \fBgenerate_credit_note\fR is provided (optionally with \fBrefund_amount\fR and/or \fBcredit_amount\fR), this validation is bypassed: the invoice is forcibly voided and a credit note is generated. If the specified refund/credit amounts do not cover the full invoice total, the remainder is issued on a second credit note that is created and immediately voided.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--credit-amount\fP=""
	Portion of the invoice amount (in cents) to be credited to the customer's balance in the generated credit note.

.PP
\fB--generate-credit-note\fP=""
	Set to 'true' to force voiding the invoice and generate a credit note.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for void

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--refund-amount\fP=""
	Portion of the invoice amount (in cents) to be refunded to the customer in the generated credit note.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
